=== Prompt for EPAM-067 (attempt 1) ===
Implement user story EPAM-067: Interactive Provider Switch Confirmation

## Story Description
Add interactive confirmation dialog when budget threshold is reached. Instead of automatic downgrade, prompt user with: (1) Visual warning that threshold reached, (2) Suggested model switch within same provider (e.g., claude-opus-4-6 → claude-sonnet-4-5), (3) Show cost comparison and remaining budget, (4) User confirms or declines, (5) On confirm, switch model while preserving conversation context. Uses cached SSO credentials - no re-auth needed. Critical for demo to show controlled provider switching with context retention.

## Acceptance Criteria
- When budget threshold reached, display visual warning with current session cost and configured limit
- Prompt shows suggested model switch within same provider (e.g., claude-opus-4-6 → claude-sonnet-4-5)
- Display cost comparison: current model cost per 1K tokens vs suggested model cost
- User can confirm (Y) or decline (N) the switch via prompts library
- On confirm, switch model while preserving full conversation context (messages, tokens, session state)
- On decline, pause and offer alternatives: end session, continue with current model, or manual model select
- Context retention verified: message history, token counts, and session state preserved after switch
- Visual confirmation shown after switch: ✓ Switched to {provider}/{model}, context retained ({N} messages)
- Uses cached SSO credentials for target model - no re-authentication required
- Unit tests cover: prompt rendering, user input handling, context preservation, model switch execution

## Technical Notes
- files: ["src/cli/repl/Repl.ts","src/cli/repl/SlashCommands.ts","src/billing/BudgetGuard.ts"]
- requiredSkills: ["TypeScript","cli-ux","prompts"]
- implementationNotes: ["Use prompts library for interactive confirmation","BudgetGuard.onHardLimit config option: \"confirm\" | \"downgrade\" | \"pause\"","Store conversation context before switch, restore after","Display: \"Session: $X.XX of $Y.YY limit | Claude: $0.003/1K tokens → Codex: $0.0001/1K tokens\"","Model switch within same provider (Codemie SSO)","Example: claude-opus-4-6 ($0.015/1K) → claude-sonnet-4-5 ($0.003/1K)","Same SSO token works for all models in account","No credential refresh needed - just update model parameter in ProviderChain"]

